{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "AI Code Review & QA Agent",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/acme/ai-code-review",
          "version": "deepseek-v4-flash",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "acr/bug",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Integer check admits values past MAX_SAFE_INTEGER"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "bug",
                  "agent"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "acr/maintainability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "saveOrder's `ok: true` flag can never be false"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "maintainability",
                  "agent"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "acr/testing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "UUID assertion matches any 36-character string"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "testing",
                  "agent"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/bug",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Integer check admits values past MAX_SAFE_INTEGER\n\n`Number.isInteger` returns true for values above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` (e.g. `Number.isInteger(2**53)` is true), where `total * (1 - discountPercent / 100)` silently loses precision and can return an amount that is off by one or more minor units. Since the docstring promises an exact integer result, use `Number.isSafeInteger(total)` so oversized inputs are rejected instead of silently mis-rounded."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 16
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.5,
            "status": "suppressed",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/bug",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "discountPercent is not required to be an integer\n\nThe docstring describes `discountPercent` as a percentage between 0 and 100, but only finiteness and range are checked, so fractional percentages such as `applyDiscount(100, 10.5)` are accepted and produce a rounded result. If fractional percentages are intended, the docstring should say so; if not, add a `Number.isInteger(discountPercent)` check so callers get a clear error rather than a silently rounded amount."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 19
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.5,
            "status": "suppressed",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/bug",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "applyDiscount rounds negative totals asymmetrically\n\n`Number.isInteger(total)` accepts negative amounts (refunds/credits), but `Math.round` rounds halves toward +Infinity, so the discount is not symmetric around zero. `applyDiscount(-1, 50)` returns `-0` (i.e. 0) instead of -1, and `applyDiscount(-3, 50)` returns -1 instead of -2 — a one-minor-unit discrepancy that only appears on negative amounts, so it will not show up in the existing all-positive tests. Fix by rounding on the magnitude, e.g. `Math.sign(total) * Math.round(Math.abs(total) * (1 - discountPercent / 100))`, or reject negative totals explicitly if refunds are out of scope."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 25
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.45,
            "status": "suppressed",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/maintainability",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "saveOrder's `ok: true` flag can never be false\n\n`saveOrder` throws on every failure path (null row, insert rejection), so the returned `ok` field is always `true`. A caller that branches on `result.ok` is writing dead code and may wrongly assume a falsy `ok` is a possible outcome. Either drop the flag and return the saved order directly, or return `{ ok: false }` on the failure paths instead of throwing — but not both."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 49
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.8,
            "status": "validated",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/testing",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "UUID assertion matches any 36-character string\n\n`/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/` accepts 36 dashes or any other 36-character string of hex/dash characters, so the test would still pass if `randomUUID()` were replaced by a constant or a malformed id. Assert the actual UUID shape, e.g. `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/`, or use `node:crypto`'s `validate`/`randomUUID` comparison."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "test/pricing.test.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 39
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.8,
            "status": "validated",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/testing",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "No test covers negative totals or fractional discounts\n\nThe rejection test only covers `100.5` totals and NaN/out-of-range discounts, and the happy-path test only uses positive totals. The negative-total rounding asymmetry and the accepted fractional `discountPercent` in `applyDiscount` are therefore untested; add cases such as `applyDiscount(-1, 50)` and `applyDiscount(100, 10.5)` to pin down the intended behaviour."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "test/pricing.test.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "info",
            "confidence": 0.4,
            "status": "suppressed",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "547daa8a-0c9e-49ca-a9d7-e4fc055c7860"
          }
        }
      ],
      "originalUriBaseIds": {
